<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>{title} | AI Coachella Valley</title>
  <meta name="description" content={description} />
  <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalUrl} />

  <meta property="og:title" content="AIQnA — Methodology and Source Documentation" />
  <meta property="og:description" content="Source documentation for the Coachella Valley's first longitudinal AI sentiment corpus. Operated by AI Coachella Valley." />
  <meta property="og:url" content={canonicalUrl} />
  <meta property="og:type" content="article" />

  <link rel="alternate" href="https://aiqna.org" title="AIQnA live experience" />

  <!-- AIQnA IQ-mark favicon — per-page override (AICV site default untouched elsewhere) -->
  <link rel="icon" href="/aiqna-favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  <link rel="icon" href="/aiqna-favicon-32x32.png" sizes="32x32" type="image/png" />
  <link rel="icon" href="/aiqna-favicon-16x16.png" sizes="16x16" type="image/png" />
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/aiqna-apple-touch-icon.png" />
  <link rel="icon" href="/aiqna-favicon.ico" sizes="any" />

  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Syne:wght@500;600;700&family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;700&family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(llcSchema, null, 2)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(techArticleSchema, null, 2)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(serviceSchema, null, 2)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema, null, 2)} />

  <style>
    :root {
      --volt: #D8FF00;
      --pine: #1B4332;
      --pine-light: #2D6A4F;
      --pine-dark: #122B22;
      --pine-tint: #C8DDB4;
      --pine-mist: #E0EDD2;
      --gunmetal: #1E1E1E;
      --sand: #FAFAF7;
      --sand-light: #FFFFFF;
      --sand-dark: #E8E5DD;
      --text-primary: var(--gunmetal);
      --text-secondary: #4A4A4A;
      --text-tertiary: #888888;
      --font-display: 'Syne', system-ui, sans-serif;
      --font-body: 'DM Sans', system-ui, sans-serif;
      --font-mono: 'DM Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    }

    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      color: var(--text-primary);
      background: var(--sand);
      line-height: 1.7;
      font-size: 16px;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
    }
    .wrap { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.5rem 4rem; }

    /* ── IQ PIVOT — wordmark treatment for brand-mark contexts ──
       Use these spans around the I and Q of AIQnA only in
       brand-mark contexts (logos, eyebrows, titles, headers).
       Never in body copy where AIQnA is part of a sentence. */
    .iq-pivot { color: var(--pine-light); }
    .iq-pivot-on-dark { color: var(--pine-tint); }
    .wordmark { font-family: var(--font-body); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }

    /* ── BREADCRUMB ──────────────────────────────────────── */
    .crumb {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px;
      color: var(--text-tertiary); letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      margin-bottom: 2rem; padding-bottom: 1rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(28, 43, 34, 0.12);
    }
    .crumb a { color: var(--pine-light); text-decoration: none; }
    .crumb a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
    .crumb .sep { color: var(--text-tertiary); margin: 0 0.5em; }

    /* ── HEADER ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .header { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
    .header-eyebrow {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px;
      color: var(--pine-light); letter-spacing: 0.16em;
      text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 500;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
    .header-eyebrow .brand {
      color: var(--pine-dark); font-weight: 700;
      text-transform: none; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 13px;
    }
    .title {
      font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 44px; font-weight: 700;
      line-height: 1.05; letter-spacing: -0.03em;
      color: var(--pine-dark); margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }
    .subtitle {
      font-size: 18px; color: var(--text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.5; margin: 0; max-width: 620px;
    }

    /* ── METADATA BAR ────────────────────────────────────── */
    .meta {
      display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1.5rem;
      padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
      background: var(--sand-light);
      border: 0.5px solid rgba(28, 43, 34, 0.12);
      border-left: 3px solid var(--volt);
      border-radius: 8px;
      margin: 2rem 0 3rem;
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px;
    }
    .meta-item { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }
    .meta-label {
      color: var(--text-tertiary); letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 10px;
    }
    .meta-value { color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 500; }
    .meta-value a { color: var(--pine-light); text-decoration: none; }
    .meta-value a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

    /* ── SECTIONS ────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .section { margin: 3rem 0; }
    .section h2 {
      font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 26px; font-weight: 600;
      line-height: 1.25; letter-spacing: -0.015em;
      color: var(--pine-dark); margin: 0 0 1rem;
      padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--pine);
      display: inline-block;
    }
    .section h3 {
      font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 19px; font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--pine-dark); margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem;
    }
    .section p { margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
    .section p.intro {
      font-size: 17px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;
    }

    /* ── LIVE CTA BLOCK ──────────────────────────────────── */
    .live-cta {
      background: var(--pine); color: var(--sand-light);
      border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem; margin: 2rem 0;
      display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;
      gap: 1.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap;
      border-left: 6px solid var(--volt);
    }
    .live-cta-text { flex: 1; min-width: 240px; }
    .live-cta-label {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--volt);
      letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 4px;
    }
    .live-cta-headline {
      font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 22px; font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--sand-light); letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }
    .live-cta-btn {
      background: var(--volt); color: var(--pine-dark);
      padding: 10px 20px; border-radius: 6px; font-weight: 600;
      text-decoration: none; font-size: 15px; white-space: nowrap;
    }

    /* ── FACT TABLE ──────────────────────────────────────── */
    .facts { margin: 1.5rem 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(28, 43, 34, 0.12); }
    .fact {
      display: grid; grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
      padding: 0.85rem 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(28, 43, 34, 0.12);
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }
    .fact-key {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-tertiary);
      letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; padding-top: 2px;
    }
    .fact-val { color: var(--text-primary); }

    /* ── PRINCIPLES LIST ─────────────────────────────────── */
    .principles { margin: 1.5rem 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
    .principles li {
      padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem 0.85rem 1.5rem;
      border-left: 3px solid var(--volt);
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
      background: var(--pine-mist);
    }
    .principles li strong {
      display: block; color: var(--pine-dark);
      font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 4px;
    }
    .principles li span { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 15px; }

    /* ── POLICIES TABLE ──────────────────────────────────── */
    .policy {
      margin: 1rem 0; padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
      background: var(--sand-light);
      border: 0.5px solid rgba(28, 43, 34, 0.12);
      border-radius: 6px;
    }
    .policy-key {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--pine-light);
      letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: 6px;
    }
    .policy-val { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.55; }

    /* ── FAQ ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .faq { margin: 2rem 0; }
    .faq-item { border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(28, 43, 34, 0.12); padding: 1.25rem 0; }
    .faq-item:first-child { border-top: 1px solid rgba(28, 43, 34, 0.12); }
    .faq-q {
      font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--pine-dark); margin: 0 0 0.5rem; line-height: 1.4;
    }
    .faq-a { margin: 0; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; }

    /* ── ENDPOINT BLOCK ──────────────────────────────────── */
    .endpoints {
      background: var(--sand-light);
      border: 0.5px solid rgba(28, 43, 34, 0.12);
      border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;
    }
    .endpoint {
      display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 1rem;
      padding: 0.5rem 0; flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .endpoint-method {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px;
      background: var(--pine); color: var(--volt);
      padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 4px; letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      font-weight: 600;
    }
    .endpoint-path {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 14px;
      color: var(--pine-dark); font-weight: 500;
    }
    .endpoint-desc { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-tertiary); flex: 1; }

    /* ── FOOTER ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .footer {
      margin-top: 4rem; padding-top: 2rem;
      border-top: 2px solid var(--pine);
      font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-tertiary); line-height: 1.7;
    }
    .footer-grid {
      display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 2rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
    .footer h4 {
      font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 14px; font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--pine-dark); margin: 0 0 0.5rem; letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    }
    .footer a { color: var(--pine-light); text-decoration: none; }
    .footer a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
    .footer-fine {
      font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-tertiary);
      padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(28, 43, 34, 0.12);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .footer-tagline {
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10.5px;
      letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--pine); text-align: center;
    }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      .wrap { padding: 1.25rem 1rem 3rem; }
      .title { font-size: 32px; }
      .subtitle { font-size: 16px; }
      .section h2 { font-size: 22px; }
      .fact { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
      .footer-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
      .live-cta { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

<main class="wrap">

  <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="https://aicoachellavalley.com/">AI Coachella Valley</a>
    <span class="sep">/</span>
    <span class="wordmark">A<span class="iq-pivot">I</span><span class="iq-pivot">Q</span>nA</span>
  </nav>

  <header class="header">
    <div class="header-eyebrow"><span class="brand">A<span class="iq-pivot">I</span><span class="iq-pivot">Q</span>nA</span> · SOURCE DOCUMENTATION · AICV INTELLIGENCE NETWORK</div>
    <h1 class="title">A<span class="iq-pivot">I</span><span class="iq-pivot">Q</span>nA</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Methodology, data handling, and aggregate findings for the Coachella Valley's first longitudinal AI sentiment corpus.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="meta">
    <div class="meta-item">
      <div class="meta-label">Operated by</div>
      <div class="meta-value">AI Coachella Valley</div>
    </div>
    <div class="meta-item">
      <div class="meta-label">Status</div>
      <div class="meta-value">{status}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="meta-item">
      <div class="meta-label">Cadence</div>
      <div class="meta-value">One question per week, 13-week series</div>
    </div>
    <div class="meta-item">
      <div class="meta-label">License</div>
      <div class="meta-value">{license}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="meta-item">
      <div class="meta-label">Live experience</div>
      <div class="meta-value"><a href="https://aiqna.org">aiqna.org</a></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p class="intro">AIQnA is a regional AI listening infrastructure operated by AI Coachella Valley. Each week, the program publishes one question about AI and daily life. Residents and business operators across the Coachella Valley respond through a short conversation with an AI agent. The aggregate findings publish every Friday in two parallel forms: a human-readable summary at aiqna.org and a structured canonical record on the AICV intelligence network at this domain.</p>
    <p>AIQnA is qualitative listening, not polling: findings surface what residents actually say about AI in their own words — a real signal and a starting point, not a representative statistical sample.</p>
    <p>The program operates as a distribution partnership with local media. Outlets distribute the weekly question through their existing channels — newsletter, on-air, print, social, web. AICV operates the conversation infrastructure, methodology, and data layer. Outlets retain the audience relationship and any local sponsorship revenue during the founding partner pilot period.</p>
    <p>AIQnA is distinct from polling. Where a poll captures a categorical response, AIQnA conducts a multi-turn conversation in which the agent listens, reacts, and reflects. This produces qualitative data — language, context, reasoning — that aggregate percentages cannot surface. Every response feeds the regional intelligence corpus and contributes to AICV's broader work of making the Coachella Valley legible to AI systems.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="live-cta">
    <div class="live-cta-text">
      <div class="live-cta-label">Take this week's question</div>
      <div class="live-cta-headline">The live <span class="wordmark">AIQnA</span> experience runs at aiqna.org</div>
    </div>
    <a href="https://aiqna.org" class="live-cta-btn">Go to aiqna.org →</a>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>The weekly cycle operates on a four-day intake, one-day publication rhythm.</p>

    <div class="facts">
      <div class="fact">
        <div class="fact-key">Monday</div>
        <div class="fact-val">The question of the week publishes across all partner channels. Each outlet receives a tracked link and the complete content kit — topline findings, word cloud, city breakdown, quotes, story-lead memo, social posts, and radio reads with a newsletter blurb.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="fact">
        <div class="fact-key">Tue – Thu</div>
        <div class="fact-val">Intake remains open. Residents respond through a short conversation with the AIQnA agent. Each respondent receives an immediate personal reflection. Anonymized records accumulate in the intelligence corpus.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="fact">
        <div class="fact-key">Thursday EOD</div>
        <div class="fact-val">Intake closes. The synthesis pass runs across that week's responses. Aggregate findings, word clouds, and city-level breakdowns are generated.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="fact">
        <div class="fact-key">Friday morning</div>
        <div class="fact-val">The results kit is delivered to all partner outlets. Findings publish at aiqna.org/results/[week] and as a structured canonical record at aicoachellavalley.com/aiqna/[week-slug].</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Methodology</h2>

    <h3>Question selection</h3>
    <p>Questions are drafted by AICV against a calendar mapped to the 13-week series structure. Each season covers the AI domains identified as most salient to Coachella Valley residents — work, education, healthcare, creativity, privacy, journalism, companionship, environment, civic services, and others. The full series rotates seasonally; the same domain may be revisited quarter over quarter to track longitudinal shifts. Exact question phrasing is not reused — published questions remain unique to their week.</p>
    <p>Questions are designed to be accessible to any resident regardless of technical background, locally specific where appropriate, and structurally neutral — they prompt reflection rather than steering toward a predetermined answer.</p>

    <h3>Conversation conduct</h3>
    <p>The AIQnA agent is built on Anthropic Managed Agents infrastructure. Each session begins with two classification questions — city of residence and whether the respondent is participating as an individual or on behalf of a business. The agent then conducts a guided conversation around the week's question. The agent listens, reacts, and probes when responses warrant follow-up. Sessions typically run six to ten exchanges and complete in under five minutes.</p>
    <p>Each respondent is asked whether their words may be published anonymously alongside aggregate findings. Opt-out preserves contribution to the aggregate while excluding verbatim publication.</p>

    <h3>Aggregation and synthesis</h3>
    <p>At the end of each intake week, a synthesis pass aggregates the structured intake records into topline findings, city-level breakdowns, and verbatim quote selections. Records flagged as anomalous or low-quality are quarantined and excluded from aggregate output. City-level breakdowns require a minimum of 25 responses for that city in that week; below this threshold, the city rolls into "other Coachella Valley" in published breakdowns.</p>

    <h3>Quote citation format</h3>
    <p>Every verbatim quote published anywhere uses the canonical attribution format:</p>
    <p style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; background: var(--sand-light); border: 0.5px solid rgba(28, 43, 34, 0.12); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: 4px;">"Anonymous Coachella Valley resident · [business type] · [city] · in response to [question_id], [date]"</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Privacy and data handling</h2>
    <p>AIQnA is designed for anonymized civic listening. Individual respondent identity is not collected, requested, or retained. The only metadata captured at intake is city and audience type.</p>

    <ul class="principles">
      <li>
        <strong>No individual identification</strong>
        <span>Name, email, phone, or other identifying information is not requested at any point. Respondents who volunteer such information have it stripped from intelligence records before storage.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No individual data sharing</strong>
        <span>Individual response records are never shared with media partners, sponsors, or any third party. Only aggregate findings, anonymized quotes, and city-level breakdowns are published.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No third-party sale</strong>
        <span>AICV does not sell, license, or otherwise transfer AIQnA data to any third party. The corpus is operated as civic infrastructure, not as a commercial dataset.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Open aggregate publication</strong>
        <span>All aggregate findings publish openly under CC-BY-4.0. The corpus is intended to be useful to journalists, researchers, policy makers, agents, and the community at large.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Trust and editorial integrity</h2>
    <p>AIQnA operates as a neutral civic listening infrastructure. Editorial integrity is structurally protected, not merely promised.</p>

    <ul class="principles">
      <li>
        <strong>Sponsor independence</strong>
        <span>Sponsors do not select questions, review findings before publication, or shape methodology. Sponsorship buys association with the program, not influence over its outputs.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Partner independence</strong>
        <span>Media partners distribute the question and publish the results but do not modify questions, edit findings, or set methodology. AICV controls the editorial chain.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Findings transparency</strong>
        <span>The methodology that produces each weekly finding is documented and reproducible. Aggregate data publishes in machine-readable form alongside the human-readable summary.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No political endorsement</strong>
        <span>AIQnA does not endorse candidates, parties, or political positions. Questions and findings are presented documentarily.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Sponsor acceptance policy</h3>
    <p>Sponsorship is open across categories — local businesses, financial institutions, educational and healthcare systems, civic anchors, foundations, technology and AI companies, data center operators, and political organizations are all eligible. The constraint is per-question, not per-industry: a sponsor may not fund a week whose question directly bears on that sponsor's own interests. A data center operator cannot sponsor a week asking about data centers; a political organization cannot sponsor a week asking about an election it is party to. This per-question conflict-of-interest rule — not a blanket industry ban — is how AIQnA keeps sponsorship independent of the questions and findings, consistent with the editorial-integrity principles above.</p>

    <h3>Rate limiting and abuse protection</h3>
    <p>AIQnA enforces one response per IP address per question via Cloudflare Turnstile and edge bot protection. Duplicate attempts receive a soft notice without revealing the limit mechanism. The synthesis agent quality-scores responses; anomalous patterns are quarantined from publication.</p>

    <h3>URL stability</h3>
    <p>Once a weekly finding publishes, the canonical URL never changes and the data never disappears. AIQnA findings are designed as citable primary sources for agents, researchers, and future AICV reports.</p>
  </section>

